        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "ANTIQUITY & CLASSICAL (600 BCE – 500 CE)\n  ─────────────────────────────────────────\n  Archimedes (287–212 BCE): lever, screw, buoyancy, siege engines\n  Vitruvius (80–15 BCE): De Architectura — synthesis of Roman engineering\n  Hero of Alexandria (10–70 CE): steam reaction engine, gear trains,\n                                  pneumatics, surveying instruments"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#005",
      "path": [
        "00-OVERVIEW.md"
