        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "INDUSTRIAL REVOLUTION (1750–1850)\n  ───────────────────────────────────\n  Watt (1736–1819): condenser steam engine, governor (feedback control)\n  Trevithick (1771–1833): high-pressure steam, first steam locomotive\n  Stephenson (1781–1848): practical railways, Rocket locomotive\n  Brunel I+II (Mark+Isambard): Great Western Railway, SS Great Britain,\n                               Clifton Suspension Bridge, Thames Tunnel"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#008",
