      },
      "text": "ELECTRICAL AGE (1830–1900)\n  ───────────────────────────\n  Faraday (1791–1867): electromagnetic induction, electric motor\n  Maxwell (1831–1879): electromagnetic theory (physics, not engineering)\n  Edison (1847–1931): electric light, DC power distribution, phonograph\n  Tesla (1856–1943): AC motors, polyphase power systems, radio\n  Westinghouse (1846–1914): AC distribution, safety brake, transformer\n  Marconi (1874–1937): practical wireless telegraphy"
    },
    {
      "id": "00-OVERVIEW.md#009",
